# The dock: the controller's end of Valve's puck's charging pads (docs/api.md, "The dock").
# Sourced from lib/opensc2/Kconfig, inside "if OPENSC2".

config OPENSC2_DOCK_LINK
	bool "Dock link: vendor commands and the state report over the puck's charging pads"
	default y if OPENSC2_TEST_HOOKS
	help
	  The dock's protocol, with no pins of its own: the 73-byte frames and their CRC, a
	  session (one request at a time; any frame that fails ends it), the probe's identity
	  record, vendor commands on a stored request of the dock's own (0x81 and 0x85 do nothing
	  there), the latest state report for GET input, attribute 11 of 0x83 = 64000 while the
	  dock is the only link, and the dock's pure rules (the pilot check, the supply rule, the
	  docked states). Its frames come from OPENSC2_DOCK's UART, or from the hardware test
	  hooks' dock ops, which test the protocol on a board with nothing wired; that is why it is
	  on by default with the hooks. While no session runs, nothing changes on USB or the radio.
	  About 3 KB of flash.

config OPENSC2_DOCK
	bool "Dock UART and pilot sense (BUILT, UNTESTED on hardware)"
	depends on $(dt_alias_enabled,opensc2-dock)
	depends on UART_ASYNC_API && ADC
	select OPENSC2_DOCK_LINK
	help
	  BUILT, NEVER RUN ON HARDWARE. Serves the puck's dock requests on a UART, 115200 baud 8N1,
	  and senses the pilot on an ADC channel (gain 1/6 of the internal reference, 12 bits, no
	  divider: present inside 2000 to 3300 mV at the pin), both named by the devicetree node
	  aliased opensc2-dock (compatible "opensc2,dock"). app/dock.conf and app/dock.overlay are
	  a SuperMini variant. The pads' voltages and loads have not been measured: nothing may be
	  connected to Valve's puck's pads without the owner's step-by-step go-ahead
	  (docs/testing.md, The dock). Needs the UART instance's async API
	  (CONFIG_UART_ASYNC_API, the instance's CONFIG_UART_<n>_ASYNC).

if OPENSC2_DOCK

config OPENSC2_DOCK_THREAD_PRIORITY
	int "Dock thread priority"
	default 9
	help
	  The real controller serves the dock at priority 9, just below its input sampling.

config OPENSC2_DOCK_THREAD_STACK_SIZE
	int "Dock thread stack size"
	default 2048
	help
	  The thread runs vendor commands, flash writes included (a pairing over the dock saves the
	  bond), as the USB stack's thread does on the cable (the blank canvas gives that one 2048
	  bytes for the same reason).

endif # OPENSC2_DOCK
